49	\textbf{Abstract.}
50	We describe an autonomous procurement agent that negotiates by e-mail with simulated suppliers
51	and concludes each case with either a single accepted term sheet or a withdrawal. Performance is
52	measured on total cost \C{} over the case horizon rather than on unit price; the agent therefore
53	optimises payment terms, delivery, contract duration, quality provisions and index clauses
54	jointly with price. The architecture separates two responsibilities. Deterministic code computes
55	every binding quantity and verifies it against the arena's cost function. A team of
56	language-model subagents analyses the supplier, rehearses the negotiation and composes the
57	correspondence, and its output is constrained by code before use. On the ten hosted practice
58	cases the agent concluded ten agreements with a mean score of 0.777.
